"""A pnpm workspace member entered through its `exports` map, not through an index.

`@npm//:pulse` is the hub target the `link:` in tests/npm/pnpm-lock.yaml
produces, and package.json here is the only statement of what each of this
member's specifiers means: `pulse` is entry.ts, `pulse/button` is four
directories down, `pulse/tokens/<name>` is a file under a
directory of another name, `pulse/internal/*` is not exported and
`pulse/theme.css` is not TypeScript at all. None of that is recoverable from the
member's directory layout, which is the whole point -- guessing
`<root>/index.d.ts` and `<root>/*` answers only the members whose entry happens
to be an index at the root, and answers a subpath only where the specifier
happens to mirror the layout.

The subtree is one target, so a subpath's declaration lands under this package's
output directory at the same depth its source sits at here.
"""

# The srcs below span these directories; a BUILD file in any of them would turn
# it into a package and make those labels cross a package boundary.
# gazelle:exclude components
# gazelle:exclude styles

load("@rules_typescript//ts:defs.bzl", "ts_compile")

# keep
ts_compile(
    name = "pulse",
    srcs = [
        "components/controls/button/index.ts",
        "entry.ts",
        "styles/tokens/color.ts",
    ],
    emit = True,  # keep
    package_scopes = ["package.json"],
    visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
)
